functions.notes:
INDEXCURVE IS CALLED ONLY WHEN `pass == 0` AND `hashing` — i.e. `if (!pass && hashing) indexCurve(ear);`. It is therefore called: (1) once from the top-level `earcutLinked(outerNode)`, and (2) once per half from `splitEarcut`, which invokes `earcutLinked(a)` / `earcutLinked(c)` with the defaulted pass 0. The pass-1 and pass-2 recursive retries do NOT re-index — they reuse the existing (possibly partially unlinked) z chain.

Crucially `hashing` (not `pass`) selects isEarHashed vs isEar, so pass 1 and 2 still use isEarHashed on a chain that was indexed during pass 0.

removeNode keeps the z chain consistent:
  p->next->prev = p->prev;
  p->prev->next = p->next;
  if (p->prevZ) p->prevZ->nextZ = p->nextZ;
  if (p->nextZ) p->nextZ->prevZ = p->prevZ;
so cut ears and filtered-out collinear points vanish from the z chain immediately. Note the removed node's own prevZ/nextZ are NOT cleared.

Nodes minted by splitPolygon (hole bridges, splitEarcut diagonals) have z == 0 and null prevZ/nextZ until an indexCurve pass adopts them; a hole-bridge node created before the top-level earcutLinked is adopted normally, whereas a splitEarcut diagonal node is adopted by the immediately following earcutLinked(a)/earcutLinked(c).

